hrough exposure</span><span class=\"n v\">$13,737</span><span class=\"of-s\">$13,466 directly · $271 through <a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"name:VXUS\">VXUS</a></span></span></div><h3 class=\"sub\">Profile</h3><div class=\"profile\"><p>Founded in 1937, Toyota is one of the world&#x27;s largest automakers, with 11.3 million units sold at retail in fiscal 2026, including 10.5 million across the Toyota and Lexus brands. Brands include Toyota, Lexus, Daihatsu, and truck maker Hino; market share in Japan is about 51% excluding minivehicles, while US share is around 15%. The firm also owns stakes in Denso, a parts supplier, about 20% of Subaru, and holds investments in many other firms, including shares of Uber Technologies, Joby Aviation, Aurora Innovation, Isuzu Motors, and about 5% in each of Mazda and Suzuki. Fiscal 2026 sales excluding financial services were JPY 46.1 trillion. Toyota also has a financing arm and manufactures homes and boats.</p><button class=\"linkish\" type=\"button\" data-more>More</button></div><dl class=fields><dt>Industry</dt><dd><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"industry:automobiles\">Automobiles</a></dd><dt>Country</dt><dd><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"country:JP\">Japan</a></dd></dl><h3 class=\"sub\">Betas</h3><table class=\"cmp \"><thead><tr><th></th><th class=\"n\">Beta</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:1\">S&amp;P 500</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">0.73</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:2\">Long Treasury yield</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">0.20</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:3\">US dollar against major currencies</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">−0.76</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:4\">Crude oil price</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">−0.06</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:5\">Semiconductor stocks</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">−0.31</span></td></tr><tr><th>